# Drizzle Schema Workflow

## When This Rule Applies

Apply this workflow **whenever the user asks to create or modify database tables** (or otherwise change the database schema: tables/columns/indexes/relations/constraints).

## The Only Rule That Matters

**AI must only modify schema files. Never generate, edit, or touch migration files.**

Migration files are owned by Drizzle, not by AI or humans.

---

## What AI Can Touch

✅ `db/schema.ts` — add/modify tables, columns, indexes, foreign keys, delete cascades  
✅ `drizzle.config.ts` — config only
✅ `.ai/database-schema.md` — keep documentation in sync with schema changes  

## What AI Must Never Touch

❌ `drizzle/meta/*.json` — Drizzle internal snapshots, always malforms if edited  
❌ `drizzle/*.sql` — generated migration SQL, never hand-edit  
❌ Running `drizzle-kit generate` or `drizzle-kit migrate` — user runs these manually  

---

## After Every Schema Change, Tell the User

When editing any schema file, also update `.ai/database-schema.md` so it reflects the latest schema.
Always end your response with:

```
Run:
  npm run db:generate
  npm run db:migrate
```
